feat: take identity out of the model's hands, and make signing one command (#170, #171, #172, #176, #177) (#178)

Collapsed from the branch it replaces, whose history named the operator's other
projects in a public repository. The measurements are kept in the file
comments; the names are gone.

IDENTITY IS ISSUED BY THE HARNESS, NOT ASKED FOR BY THE MODEL. #170 splits the
five tools across two listeners: register_agent, record_event and retire_agent
answer only on the admin listener the model's client is never pointed at, and
8080 keeps the two tools that need a run_id somebody else issued. A withheld
tool is absent, not broken -- it must not appear in MissingTools, or a
deployment cannot tell a deliberate split from a missing binding (MCP-024..027).
An unknown name in the list is refused outright (MCP-028), because a compose
file with a typo would otherwise start with four tools and look exactly like a
deliberate split.

The harness hook registers a subagent at SubagentStart and blocks if it cannot
(IP §6.1), retires at SubagentStop without ever blocking -- exit 2 there
produced a nine-deep retry storm -- and records observed tool calls as digests.
SessionStart gives the operator's own session an identity too, and that one
never blocks: refusing a subagent costs nothing, refusing the human stops them
working on their own machine.

SIGNING IS ONE COMMAND. scripts/innsegl-commit.sh replaces four MCP calls made
by hand, refuses rather than falling back to an unsigned commit, and carries two
idempotency keys -- one per attempt so a retry can get a live run, one per
content so the same tree cannot produce two commits. scripts/verify-branch.sh
gates the merge on it. `make start`, `make link` and `make sign` are the whole
interface, and the compose override signs in the working tree instead of a copy.

TWO THINGS THAT WERE LOSING DATA. The proof API served an allowlist holding only
the demo repository, so every proof request about a real one answered 404 --
which reads as a verdict about the commit and was a statement about the
configuration (#177). And rekor mints a new Trillian tree whenever tlog_id is 0,
so every restart moved the log to an empty tree and stranded the entries under
the old id: three trees, 7 + 43 + 0 leaves, the empty one being served (#176).
ADR-0028 pinned the log's key so a restart could not change who the log is;
nothing pinned which tree it serves. Both are fixed and the entries are back.

Also: the runs table sorts in the ledger rather than in one fetched page, the
sealer and reconciler can run inside the MCP process, the reaper finally runs at
all, and the dashboard has a mark.

ADR-0045 is proposed and NOT accepted: repo, branch and parent_run_id belong on
run_registered, which is a protected surface and a major release.

